<div id="recipe-85083-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Yields:</strong> This recipe makes 4 doner kebab wraps ideal for serving four adults. The nutritional values below are per serving.</li>
<li><strong>Storing leftovers:&nbsp;</strong>If you know you&rsquo;ll have leftovers, I recommend storing all components of the recipe separately in airtight containers. If stored in the fridge, they should be good for up to 3-4 days.<br>You can store the wraps as well, but I recommend consuming them in the next day or two. You can reheat in a low-heat (300&deg;F) oven until warmed to your liking.</li>
<li>Some versions of this recipe divide the doner meat mixture into 4 pieces (instead of 3 as I did) for 1 pound of ground meat. During my testing, I thought the doner meat made with 4 pieces was too thin to my liking, but either way would work.</li>
</ul>
